  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting good environmental governance and the protection of natural resources in Peru</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Red Muqui is a Peruvian civil society coalition working on the social impact of mining. It has 27 members, including key CAFOD partner CEAS, the Social Action Commission of the Peruvian Bishops&#x2019; Conference and ten other-Church based groups. The project aims to protect human rights and natural resources in Peru in order to ensure sustainable development, which takes into account the needs of the local population.</narrative>
  </description>
